        "department": null,
        "description": "The GDP contribution of services sector in the Global as well as the Indian economy is the highest. Consequently, the service sector is the largest employment generator. Marketing is a critical contributor to success of service organizations and many job profiles (including those in product marketing) require reasonable service marketing interventions. This course will empower and equip the student with concepts for these interventions and for facing the inherent challenges in marketing services.\n\nThe course apprises the student with the differentiating concepts and characteristics of service marketing and the related variant consumer behaviour. It outlines the framework for understanding customer requirements, expectations, and perception of services. It enables the student to create winning strategies, design customer focused offerings and detail implementable marketing programs for success in the services marketplace. The course equips the student with tools and techniques essential for managing service delivery standards for customer satisfaction and growth.\n\nA domain specific overview of a practicing expert is also envisaged on financial services, IT Services, online retailing, Hospitality and healthcare services in this course. The course enables students to find specific job profiles in these domains. The course has a strong focus on technology use in services",
